  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Ice Castles** (2 reviews): Listener notes the opener is from the White Pepper album, transitioning well into Fiesta; The listener calls the opening track a kickass way to start the show [3][5]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Pony**: back after 63 archived shows (1104 days) [6]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **ween2007-10-26** (recommended): matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 29 songs; 139 min [1]\n- **ween2007-10-26.oktava.shnf**: source not stated; 30 songs; 140 min; rated 3.33/5 by 3 [2]. Said about its sound: Recording features slight adjustments to highs and mids, with the reviewer praising the overall sound quality [4]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The reviewer describes the audience at the venue as being great [4]\n- Claude broke his snare drum during the performance, which the listener found awesome [5]\n- The band is described as being on fire during this specific fall and winter tour [3]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **ween2007-10-26**: taped by Sparki; transferred by Sparki; source: Akg 480 ck61 > Lunatec V2 @30db > Tacscam Da-P1 @ 44.1khz (Located left side at front edge of SBD) [1]. Also: Transferred via Sony DTC-690, Audioquest Optilink, and Sekd'D Prodif Plus to Samplitude software [1]\n- **ween2007-10-26.oktava.shnf**: taped by BradM; transferred by BradM; source: matched Oktava MC-012 (cardioid,90*/30cm,FOB,5'LOC,8'up) > Edirol UA-5 (Oade digi-mod,44.1kHz) > optical > Creative Nomad JB3 (WAV) [2]",
